WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
A splash of fresh water will reach the depths of your heart. Those mighty blue waves can propel you forward or they can calm and soothe. Coast to Michigan coast. Simply feel the flow in the moment. And let those vast lakes, rivers and streams create everlasting memories. Jump right in and let fresh wash over you in Pure Michigan. Keep it fresh at Michigan.org. Or on our website.
清凉的泉水会触动你的心弦。那汹涌的蓝色波浪既能推动你前行，也能让你平静舒缓。从密歇根的这一岸到那一岸。只需感受当下的流动。让那些广阔的湖泊、河流和溪流创造永恒的记忆。纵身跃入，让清凉在纯净的密歇根洗涤你的身心。在 Michigan.org 保持清爽。或访问我们的网站。

2
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:53.000
34-year-old Sherry Papini knew the lyrics to everything by pop singer Michael Buble well. Not only had she chosen it as her wedding song when marrying the love of her life, Keith, it was also a great pace keeper when exercising. In November 2016, the Californian mother of two had almost fully healed from a recent breast augmentation procedure. Finally feeling well enough to start jogging again, Sherry had started training for an upcoming 5K race. Still a bit rusty, she was using an app to track her progress. Wednesday, November 2 was a clear day. With her two young children in daycare and her husband at work,
34 岁的雪莉·帕皮尼（Sherry Papini）对流行歌手迈克尔·布雷（Michael Buble）的所有歌词都烂熟于心。这不仅是她与挚爱基思（Keith）结婚时的婚礼歌曲，也是她锻炼时保持节奏的绝佳伴侣。2016 年 11 月，这位加州二胎妈妈刚从最近的隆胸手术中基本康复。终于感觉身体状况良好，可以重新开始慢跑，雪莉开始为即将到来的 5 公里长跑比赛进行训练。由于还有些生疏，她正在使用一款应用程序来追踪自己的进度。11 月 2 日，星期三，天气晴朗。她的两个年幼的孩子在托儿所，丈夫在上班，

3
00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Sherry got dressed in black leggings, a pink Nike hoodie and checkered tennis shoes. She headed outside. The Papini family lived in Redding, a small city in Northern California. Their home in the rural Mountain Gate area was surrounded by flat tree-lined roads and wide open spaces that provided a pleasant backdrop for a run. Sherry connected her earbuds to her iPhone and opened her fitness app. She pressed play on her wedding song and started jogging down her driveway. Music
雪莉穿上黑色紧身裤、粉色耐克连帽衫和格子网球鞋。她走出门外。帕皮尼一家住在北加州的一个小城市雷丁（Redding）。他们在农村山门（Mountain Gate）地区的家被平坦的林荫道路和广阔的空地所环绕，为跑步提供了宜人的背景。雪莉将耳机连接到 iPhone 上，打开了健身应用程序。她按下婚礼歌曲的播放键，开始沿着车道慢跑。音乐

4
00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:51.000
Later that evening, an emergency services operator received a call from Sherry's husband, Keith Papini. He'd just returned home from work and said he was freaking out because his wife wasn't there. Officers from the Shasta County Sheriff's Office quickly arrived at the couple's home. Keith explained that it was just after 5pm when he pulled into the driveway of his family's two-story home. It was the same house that Keith himself had been raised in. With its sprawling backyard, leafy surrounds and basketball ring in the driveway, it was the ideal place to raise a family. Keith approached the front door, prepared for the usual warm welcome from his boisterous 4-year-old son and 2-year-old daughter. But as he stepped inside, it was oddly quiet.
那天晚上晚些时候，紧急服务接线员接到了雪莉丈夫基思·帕皮尼的电话。他刚下班回家，说他快疯了，因为他的妻子不在家。沙斯塔县警长办公室的警官很快赶到了这对夫妇的家中。基思解释说，下午 5 点刚过，他开车驶入自家两层楼房的车道。这正是基思从小长大的房子。这里有宽敞的后院、绿树成荫的环境和车道上的篮球架，是抚养家庭的理想之地。基思走向前门，准备迎接他那 4 岁儿子和 2 岁女儿通常的热情欢迎。但当他走进屋内时，却异常安静。

5
00:03:51.000 --> 00:04:40.000
Sherry Papini typically kept the family on a tight schedule and always let her husband know if anything unexpected had arisen. But Keith said the last he'd heard from Sherry was around 11am when she texted asking if he was going to be home for lunch. It had been a busy day for Keith, who worked at a Best Buy electronic store and he'd responded that he wouldn't be able to make it. Keith walked through their home. Everything appeared as normal except for a half-wrapped present addressed to him from Sherry and the kids. Inside was a handmade American flag pillow. Keith looked outside. Sherry's car was in the driveway, but there was no sign of her or the kids anywhere.
雪莉·帕皮尼通常让家里保持严格的时间表，如果发生任何意外，她总是会通知丈夫。但基思说，他最后一次收到雪莉的消息是在上午 11 点左右，当时她发短信问他是否会回家吃午饭。对于在百思买（Best Buy）电子商店工作的基思来说，那是忙碌的一天，他回复说他赶不回来。基思走过他们的家。一切看起来都很正常，除了一个半包装好的礼物，上面写着是雪莉和孩子们送给他的。里面是一个手工制作的美国国旗枕头。基思向外看去。雪莉的车在车道上，但无论哪里都没有她或孩子们的踪影。

6
00:04:40.000 --> 00:05:29.000
He sent Sherry a text, but there was no response. He called the children's daycare provider and asked what time Sherry had stopped by. The daycare worker was taken aback. Sherry hadn't picked the kids up. They were still there. Keith's initial confusion quickly turned to concern. He logged in to his Find My iPhone app, which was also configured to recognize the location of his wife's device. The icon confirmed that Sherry's phone was located less than one mile away at the corner of Old Oregon Trail and Sunrise Drive. Thinking Sherry might have gone for a walk, Keith drove to the specified location.
他给雪莉发了短信，但没有回复。他打电话给孩子们的托儿所老师，询问雪莉是什么时候去接孩子的。托儿所工作人员感到很惊讶。雪莉并没有去接孩子。他们还在那里。基思最初的困惑很快变成了担忧。他登录了自己的“查找我的 iPhone”应用程序，该程序也配置为识别他妻子设备的位置。图标显示雪莉的手机位于不到一英里外的老俄勒冈小径（Old Oregon Trail）和日出大道（Sunrise Drive）的拐角处。基思以为雪莉可能去散步了，于是开车前往指定地点。

7
00:05:29.000 --> 00:06:12.000
There was no one there. He called his mother to see if she had spoken to Sherry. She hadn't. Keith tried to remain calm. He told himself that Sherry might have accidentally left her phone on the roof of her car and it had fallen off during the drive. But that didn't explain why she hadn't picked up the kids. Sherry was an incredibly dedicated mother who doted on her children and it was completely out of character for her to leave them in daycare this late. Nor did she have any health conditions that could explain a sudden absence.
那里没有人。他打电话给母亲，看她是否和雪莉谈过。她没有。基思试图保持冷静。他告诉自己，雪莉可能不小心把手机落在了车顶上，开车时掉了下来。但这并不能解释她为什么没有去接孩子。雪莉是一位极其敬业的母亲，非常疼爱她的孩子，把他们留在托儿所这么晚完全不符合她的性格。她也没有任何健康状况可以解释这种突然的缺席。

8
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:56.000
Keith got out of the car and started looking around. The intersection housed all the letter boxes for the neighborhood and it was just one and a half miles from the nearest highway. Other than that, it was fairly remote. No houses were in the immediate vicinity and traffic wasn't busy. Just off the road, Keith found Sherry's iPhone in the grass. It had a crack on the front screen but was still functioning. Sherry's headphones were still connected and Michael Buble's Everything was playing on repeat. Wrapped around the headphones were several strands of long blonde hair.
基思下了车，开始四处寻找。这个十字路口设有该社区所有的信箱，距离最近的高速公路只有一英里半。除此之外，这里相当偏僻。附近没有房屋，交通也不繁忙。在路边，基思在草丛中发现了雪莉的 iPhone。它的前屏幕有裂纹，但仍能正常工作。雪莉的耳机还连着，迈克尔·布雷的《Everything》正在循环播放。耳机上缠绕着几缕长长的金发。

9
00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:45.000
The same color and length as Sherry's. Officers visited the location where Sherry's phone was found. They found no signs that a struggle had taken place. Similarly, a search of the Pepini's home revealed that everything was in order and nothing appeared to have been stolen. But there was no evidence to support the possibility that Sherry had taken off voluntarily. Her purse and belongings were all accounted for and she hadn't made any significant withdrawals from her bank account. Police questioned whether Sherry could have run away to start afresh elsewhere. Keith vehemently denied this possibility.
颜色和长度与雪莉的一样。警官们走访了发现雪莉手机的地点。他们没有发现任何发生过搏斗的迹象。同样，对帕皮尼家的搜查显示一切井然有序，没有任何东西被盗。但没有证据支持雪莉是自愿离开的可能性。她的钱包和财物都在，而且她的银行账户也没有任何大额取款记录。警方质疑雪莉是否可能为了重新开始而离家出走。基思强烈否认了这种可能性。

10
00:07:45.000 --> 00:08:40.000
He had known Sherry since middle school. The two had shared a kiss as teenagers but it wasn't until years later that they reconnected and a romance blossomed. Keith was immediately smitten with Sherry, a bubbly blue-eyed blonde with a luminous smile. They married in 2009 and Sherry soon left her job as a telecommunications account executive to be a stay-at-home mum. It was a position she thrived in. Sherry organised all kinds of projects and activities for her children while also being a doting wife and homemaker. She put great care and attention into everything she did, be it decorating a homemade pie, planning a birthday party for her children or maintaining her physical appearance. According to Keith, the couple had a very happy marriage.
他从中学起就认识雪莉了。两人在青少年时期曾有过一次亲吻，但直到多年后他们才重新联系上，并萌生了恋情。基思立刻被雪莉迷住了，她是一个有着明亮笑容、蓝眼睛的金发女郎。他们于 2009 年结婚，雪莉很快辞去了电信客户主管的工作，成为了一名全职妈妈。这是一个她非常胜任的职位。雪莉为孩子们组织了各种项目和活动，同时也是一位疼爱丈夫的家庭主妇。她对所做的每一件事都倾注了极大的关怀和关注，无论是装饰自制的馅饼、为孩子们策划生日派对，还是保持自己的外表。据基思说，这对夫妇的婚姻非常幸福。

11
00:08:40.000 --> 00:09:35.000
They fought occasionally but no more than any other couple. Their last argument had been a month prior over something as trivial as a messy room. Keith said there was no way that Sherry would ever voluntarily leave her children. It was a sentiment shared by others who described Sherry Papini as a super mum. In the lead-up to her disappearance, everything had been completely normal. Sherry had given no indication that she was making plans to leave or wanted to escape her responsibilities. She had recently taken her children out trick-or-treating for Halloween and was already planning what to cook for an upcoming Thanksgiving dinner. A background check revealed no known history of domestic abuse or any police call-outs to the Papini's property.
他们偶尔会吵架，但并不比其他任何夫妇多。他们上一次争吵是在一个月前，因为房间凌乱这样琐碎的事情。基思说，雪莉绝不可能自愿离开她的孩子。这种观点也得到了其他人的认同，他们将雪莉·帕皮尼描述为一位“超级妈妈”。在她失踪前夕，一切都完全正常。雪莉没有任何迹象表明她正在计划离开或想要逃避责任。她最近刚带孩子们出去参加万圣节的“不给糖就捣蛋”活动，并且已经在计划感恩节晚餐要煮什么了。背景调查显示，帕皮尼家没有任何已知的家庭暴力史，也没有任何警察接到过关于帕皮尼家财产的报警。

12
00:09:35.000 --> 00:10:28.000
In fact, Keith's record was squeaky clean. Still, police had to consider the possibility that Keith was involved with his wife's disappearance. What if he had killed her and then staged a kidnapping to deflect attention from himself? Police looked into Keith's movements from Wednesday, November 2 and confirmed that he was at work all day. The last reported sighting of Sherry Papini occurred around 2pm when a neighbour saw her jogging. There had been no suspicious vehicles sighted in the area nor had anyone heard cries for help. Sherry was considered to be an alert aware person. Had someone approached her, Sherry's loved ones believed she would have put up a fight.
事实上，基思的记录非常清白。尽管如此，警方还是必须考虑基思与他妻子失踪有关的可能性。如果他杀了她，然后策划了一起绑架案来转移对自己的注意力呢？警方调查了基思在 11 月 2 日星期三的行踪，证实他整天都在上班。最后一次有人看到雪莉·帕皮尼是在下午 2 点左右，当时一位邻居看到她在慢跑。该地区没有发现可疑车辆，也没有人听到呼救声。雪莉被认为是一个警觉且有意识的人。如果有人接近她，雪莉的亲人相信她会进行反抗。

13
00:10:28.000 --> 00:11:18.000
It therefore seemed more likely that whoever took her had snuck up unsuspectingly. Either that or more than one person was involved. A team searched overnight covering a half-mile radius from the corner of Old Oregon Trail and Sunrise Drive where Sherry's phone was found. An aerial search was also conducted but nothing of interest was found. The discarded iPhone was the only clue police had to go by. The following day Sherry's sister-in-law Suzanne discussed its significance in the press, saying that while it was good to have some sort of clue, it indicated that Sherry had been taken. Suzanne said,
因此，更有可能的是，带走她的人是悄悄接近的。要么就是不止一个人参与其中。一个团队彻夜搜查了以发现雪莉手机的老俄勒冈小径和日出大道拐角处为中心半英里半径的区域。还进行了空中搜查，但没有发现任何有价值的线索。被丢弃的 iPhone 是警方唯一的线索。第二天，雪莉的嫂子苏珊（Suzanne）在媒体上讨论了它的重要性，她说虽然有一些线索是好事，但这表明雪莉是被带走的。苏珊说，

14
00:11:18.000 --> 00:12:07.000
She wouldn't just drop her phone if she was running away. At least it's giving us some kind of information but we're sick. This is a pretty sickening situation. The redding community was in shock. Sherry had no known enemies. Keith Pepini said there had been no strange activity such as suspicious calls or emails in the lead-up to his wife's disappearance. So who would abduct an innocent mother of two so brazenly in broad daylight just one mile from her home? The Milton Gate area was considered a safe place to live but like any other town, redding had skeletons in its closet.
如果她是离家出走，她不会就这样扔掉手机。至少这给了我们某种信息，但我们感到恶心。这是一种非常令人作呕的情况。雷丁社区感到震惊。雪莉没有已知的敌人。基思·帕皮尼说，在他妻子失踪前夕，没有任何奇怪的活动，如可疑的电话或电子邮件。那么，谁会在光天化日之下，在离家仅一英里远的地方，如此明目张胆地绑架一位无辜的二胎母亲呢？山门地区被认为是一个安全的居住地，但像其他任何城镇一样，雷丁也有不可告人的秘密。

15
00:12:07.000 --> 00:13:04.000
Back in August 1998, 16-year-old Tara Smith set out for a jog down Old Oregon Trail and was never seen again. While Tara's case remained unsolved, the people of Redding had never forgotten it. Some were quick to point out in eerie coincidence. Tara Smith and Sherry Pepini had attended the same high school at the same time. They also shared a similar look, with some noting they could easily pass for sisters. Although the pair weren't known to be friends and despite 18 years passing between the two disappearances, it did spark some questions. Was it possible the same perpetrator had struck again? The sex offenders lived within one mile of the location where Sherry's phone was found.
早在 1998 年 8 月，16 岁的塔拉·史密斯（Tara Smith）出发去老俄勒冈小径慢跑，从此再也没有出现过。虽然塔拉的案件仍未解决，但雷丁的人民从未忘记。有些人很快指出这是一种令人毛骨悚然的巧合。塔拉·史密斯和雪莉·帕皮尼曾在同一时间就读于同一所高中。她们的长相也很相似，有些人注意到她们很容易被误认为是姐妹。虽然这对两人是否是朋友不得而知，尽管两次失踪之间相隔了 18 年，但这确实引发了一些疑问。是否可能是同一个作案者再次作案？性犯罪者住在发现雪莉手机地点的一英里内。

16
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:49.000
Fifty more lived in the five miles beyond. Police began looking into each individual, but one by one they were all ruled out. Meanwhile, Keith Pepini agreed to participate in a polygraph test. But he was telling the truth when he said he wasn't involved in his wife's disappearance. This, along with Keith's confirmed alibi and the lack of physical evidence linking him to the crime scene, gave police the confidence to conclusively rule him out as a suspect. Being publicly cleared provided Keith with little relief. He told People Magazine,
在接下来的五英里内还住着五十人。警方开始调查每一个人，但一个接一个，他们都被排除了。与此同时，基思·帕皮尼同意参加测谎仪测试。但他确实在说实话，他说他没有参与妻子的失踪。这一点，加上基思被证实的不在场证明，以及缺乏将他与犯罪现场联系起来的物证，使警方有信心最终将他排除在嫌疑人之外。被公开洗清嫌疑并没有给基思带来多少宽慰。他告诉《人物》杂志，

17
00:13:49.000 --> 00:14:40.000
That is not where my head has been this whole time. My head has been trying to find my wife. Police continue to explore all avenues, including the possibility that Sherry might have voluntarily run away. But as the days passed with no breakthroughs, local residents became consumed by fear. They rallied behind the Pepini family, setting up a GoFundMe account to help with expenses. Missing person posters were plastered around town, urging people to be on the lookout for the 34-year-old. At a fence on the corner of Old Oregon Trail and Sunrise Drive, concerned citizens hung a bunch of helium balloons with the words, bring Sherry home, written on them.
这并不是我这段时间以来一直想的事情。我的心思一直都在试图找到我的妻子。警方继续探索所有途径，包括雪莉可能自愿离家出走的可能性。但随着日子一天天过去，没有任何突破，当地居民陷入了恐惧之中。他们支持帕皮尼一家，设立了一个 GoFundMe 账户来帮助支付费用。失踪人员海报贴满了全城，敦促人们留意这位 34 岁的女性。在老俄勒冈小径和日出大道拐角处的围栏上，忧心忡忡的市民挂了一束氦气球，上面写着“带雪莉回家”。

18
00:14:40.000 --> 00:15:27.000
A $50,000 reward for information was announced. The Pepini family hired a private investigator who began working on the possibility that Sherry had been abducted as part of a human trafficking ring. The Pepini's house was only a few miles from the Interstate 5 freeway, an area known to be used for criminal activity by Mexican cartels. A trailer near their house was also a known drug den. Maybe someone frequenting the trailer had spotted Sherry and recognized her as an easy target. Police were quick to dispel this theory. Victims of sex trafficking are typically young and childless.
悬赏 5 万美元征集线索。帕皮尼一家聘请了一名私家侦探，开始调查雪莉可能作为人口贩卖团伙的一部分被绑架的可能性。帕皮尼家距离 5 号州际公路只有几英里，该地区以墨西哥贩毒集团的犯罪活动而闻名。他们家附近的一个拖车屋也是一个已知的毒窝。也许经常出入那个拖车屋的人发现了雪莉，并认为她是一个容易下手的目标。警方很快反驳了这一理论。性贩卖的受害者通常是年轻且没有孩子的。

19
00:15:27.000 --> 00:16:19.000
But as others argued, Sherry looked notably young for her age. At five-foot-three inches tall with the petite 105-pound frame and long-blonde hair, some believed Sherry could pass for 18. Had she been targeted at random, it was possible the perpetrator had mistaken her for a much younger woman. By November 17, Sherry Pepini had been missing for 15 days. The FBI became involved as the local rumor mill swung into overdrive. Some theorized that Sherry could have been taken by a stalker. What if someone had been watching her movements closely and knew exactly when she'd be alone on the remote running trail?
但正如其他人所争辩的那样，雪莉看起来比实际年龄年轻得多。她身高 5 英尺 3 英寸，体重 105 磅，身材娇小，留着长长的金发，有些人认为雪莉看起来像 18 岁。如果她是随机被盯上的，作案者很有可能把她误认为是一个年轻得多的女性。到 11 月 17 日，雪莉·帕皮尼已经失踪 15 天了。随着当地谣言四起，联邦调查局（FBI）介入了调查。有些人推测雪莉可能被跟踪者带走了。如果有人一直在密切观察她的行踪，并且确切地知道她什么时候会独自出现在偏僻的跑步小径上呢？

20
00:16:19.000 --> 00:17:08.000
There was also talk of a possible affair. Some speculated that Sherry could have been involved with a married man whose scorned lover had abducted her as part of a revenge plot. Despite Keith Pepini being publicly cleared, many members of the public continued to cast suspicion on him. Keith Pepini did his best to hold it together for the sake of his young children. He held onto hopes that Sherry was still alive and being held somewhere. Making a teary appeal to his wife on television, Keith said, If Sherry is listening, I want to say that we are trying. We're trying the best we can and I'm so sorry that I'm not there.
还有关于可能存在婚外情的传言。一些人推测雪莉可能与一名已婚男子有染，而该男子的嫉妒情人为了报复绑架了她。尽管基思·帕皮尼被公开洗清了嫌疑，但许多公众成员继续对他表示怀疑。基思·帕皮尼为了年幼的孩子们，尽力保持坚强。他怀揣着雪莉还活着并被关在某处的希望。基思在电视上向妻子发出泪流满面的呼吁，他说：“如果雪莉在听，我想说我们正在努力。我们正在尽我们所能，我很抱歉我不在那里。”

21
00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:54.000
I love you. Addressing the perpetrator directly, Keith told People Magazine, I just want her back and I want her back safe. Just bring her home. Please bring her back. The sooner, the better. A wealthy businessman was passing through Reading when he learned of Sherry's disappearance and heard Keith's heartfelt pleas for her safe return. Something about the case struck a chord with the man. Even though he didn't know Sherry or the Pepini family, the pain they were experiencing seemed unimaginable. He began thinking about ways that he could help out.
“我爱你。”基思直接向作案者喊话，告诉《人物》杂志：“我只想让她回来，我只想让她平安回来。把她带回家。请把她带回来。越快越好。”一位富有的商人在路过雷丁时得知了雪莉失踪的消息，并听到了基思为她平安归来而发出的衷心恳求。这件事触动了这位男子的心弦。尽管他不认识雪莉或帕皮尼一家，但他们所经历的痛苦似乎是无法想象的。他开始思考自己可以提供什么帮助。

22
00:17:54.000 --> 00:18:50.000
That's when the idea struck him. What about a reverse ransom? After reaching out to Keith Pepini and getting the go ahead, the businessman who chose to remain anonymous created a website titled SherryPepini.com. He made a bizarre offer to whoever had abducted Sherry. Return her safely and receive an undisclosed six-figure reward with no questions asked. The donor wrote, I am willing to pay you in whatever way you can creatively think about where you feel safe and where nothing can be tracked to you. I will not communicate with the police and sheriff's department regarding any details about this offer. Law enforcement were firmly against this tactic for several reasons.
就在那时，他想到了一个主意。反向赎金怎么样？在联系了基思·帕皮尼并获得许可后，这位选择保持匿名的商人创建了一个名为 SherryPepini.com 的网站。他向绑架雪莉的人提出了一个奇怪的提议。平安归还她，即可获得一笔未公开的六位数奖金，且不问任何问题。捐赠者写道：“我愿意以任何你能想到的创造性方式支付给你，只要你觉得安全，且无法追踪到你。我不会就此提议的任何细节与警察和警长部门进行沟通。”执法部门坚决反对这种策略，原因有几点。

23
00:18:50.000 --> 00:19:45.000
For one, there still wasn't enough evidence to unequivocally confirm that Sherry Pepini had been abducted. If she had, her kidnapper had made no attempt to demand any kind of ransom. Two, releasing an offer like this left the Pepini family vulnerable to scam artists. And thirdly, financially rewarding someone for their criminal activity only served to encourage future copycats. The anonymous donor was undeterred. He hired an independent hostage negotiator named Cameron Gamble to act as his spokesman and gave a deadline of 100 hours, writing on his website, Once I leave town, this offer is off the table. Public reaction to the offer was mixed.
首先，仍然没有足够的证据明确证实雪莉·帕皮尼是被绑架的。如果她是，绑架者也没有试图索要任何形式的赎金。其次，发布这样的提议使帕皮尼一家容易受到诈骗者的伤害。第三，在经济上奖励某人的犯罪活动只会助长未来的模仿者。匿名捐赠者并没有被吓倒。他聘请了一位名叫卡梅伦·甘布尔（Cameron Gamble）的独立人质谈判专家作为他的发言人，并设定了 100 小时的最后期限，他在网站上写道：“一旦我离开城镇，这个提议就作废。”公众对该提议的反应不一。

24
00:19:45.000 --> 00:20:55.000
Some viewed it as a novel way to help solve missing person cases. Skeptics believed it was nothing more than a publicity stunt for Cameron Gamble to promote his hostage negotiation business. Either way, the 100 hour deadline came and went without anyone coming forward. The donor withdrew the controversial reverse ransom offer, but said the unclaimed money would be added towards the existing $50,000 reward offered by law enforcement. By November 23, Sherry Pepini had been missing for three weeks. Investigators had chased over 400 leads and executed 20 search warrants to obtain data relating to cell phone records, social media accounts, banking information and emails. A check of Sherry Pepini's cell phone revealed she had recently deleted a text message exchange with a female contact. But when police looked into this contact, they realized it wasn't a woman at all.
有些人认为这是一种解决失踪人口案件的新颖方法。怀疑论者认为这只不过是卡梅伦·甘布尔为推广其人质谈判业务而进行的宣传噱头。无论如何，100 小时的最后期限过去了，没有人站出来。捐赠者撤回了有争议的反向赎金提议，但表示未领取的钱款将增加到执法部门提供的现有 5 万美元悬赏金中。到 11 月 23 日，雪莉·帕皮尼已经失踪三周了。调查人员追踪了 400 多条线索，并执行了 20 份搜查令，以获取与手机记录、社交媒体账户、银行信息和电子邮件相关的数据。对雪莉·帕皮尼手机的检查显示，她最近删除了一段与一位女性联系人的短信交流。但当警方调查这位联系人时，他们意识到这根本不是一个女人。

25
00:20:55.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Sherry had been conversing with a man from Michigan named Donovan, but had hidden his number under a woman's name. The two had been texting between October 29 and November 1, the day before Sherry went missing. Donovan had been in San Francisco for a work conference, and the two discussed the possibility of meeting up in Reading. However, it was a five hour drive between the two cities, which Donovan deemed too far. Their rendezvous didn't eventuate, but for investigators, this was a solid lead. What if Donovan had decided to swing by Reading after all? They obtained Donovan's travel records and confirmed that he had returned to Michigan on November 2, the day of Sherry's disappearance. Investigators flew to Michigan to visit Donovan's apartment while he was at work.
雪莉一直在与一名来自密歇根州名叫多诺万（Donovan）的男子交谈，但将他的号码隐藏在一个女性名字下。两人在 10 月 29 日至 11 月 1 日（雪莉失踪前一天）期间一直在发短信。多诺万当时在旧金山参加一个工作会议，两人讨论了在雷丁见面的可能性。然而，两个城市之间有五个小时的车程，多诺万认为太远了。他们的会面没有实现，但对调查人员来说，这是一个可靠的线索。如果多诺万最终决定顺道去雷丁呢？他们获得了多诺万的旅行记录，证实他已于 11 月 2 日（雪莉失踪当天）返回密歇根州。调查人员飞往密歇根州，在多诺万上班时走访了他的公寓。

26
00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:58.000
They searched the premises, but found no sign of Sherry Pepini or anything else incriminating. When police arrived at Donovan's work for an interview, he seemed shocked. According to Donovan, he had met Sherry Pepini in 2011 when she was in Michigan for a work trip. He later told the Sacramento Bee that he found her to be, quote, drop dead gorgeous. Donovan said there was something pretty magical about her. Sherry made no mention of the fact that she was married and the two had spent the weekend together. Over the years, they continued to send the occasional flirty message, but it never went beyond that. Donovan assumed the recent contact from Sherry was due to her seeing his social media post about being in San Francisco.
他们搜查了住所，但没有发现雪莉·帕皮尼的踪迹或任何其他有罪的证据。当警察到达多诺万的工作地点进行采访时，他显得很震惊。据多诺万说，他是在 2011 年雪莉去密歇根出差时认识她的。他后来告诉《萨克拉门托蜜蜂报》，他觉得她“美得惊人”。多诺万说她身上有一种非常神奇的东西。雪莉没有提到她已婚的事实，两人度过了一个周末。多年来，他们偶尔会发送一些调情的短信，但从未超越过这一点。多诺万认为雪莉最近的联系是因为她看到了他在社交媒体上发布的关于他在旧金山的消息。

27
00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:59.000
Donovan denied being anywhere near Reading on the day Sherry went missing. He had data on his cell phone to prove he was in San Francisco at the time and others were able to confirm his alibi. For investigators, this was a major blow. It was back to the drawing board. Thursday, November 24 was Thanksgiving Day. What was typically a day of celebration for the Pepini family was now a stark reminder that 22 days had passed with no sign of Sherry. Before her disappearance, she'd been enthusiastically making plans with her in-laws about the day. She'd intended on making sweet potatoes, her children's favorite. Instead, members of the Reading community planned to gather later in the afternoon to show support for Sherry's loved ones.
多诺万否认在雪莉失踪当天出现在雷丁附近。他手机上的数据证明他当时在旧金山，其他人也能够证实他的不在场证明。对调查人员来说，这是一个重大打击。一切又回到了原点。11 月 24 日星期四是感恩节。对于帕皮尼一家来说，这通常是一个庆祝的日子，但现在却是一个严酷的提醒：22 天过去了，依然没有雪莉的踪影。在她失踪前，她曾热情地与公婆计划这一天。她打算做红薯，这是孩子们的最爱。相反，雷丁社区的成员计划在下午晚些时候聚集在一起，以表达对雪莉亲人的支持。

28
00:23:59.000 --> 00:26:10.000
Keith Pepini got up before dawn to begin his day. He was in the bathroom shaving when his phone rang. On the other line was one of the detectives working on his wife's case. They finally had news. Sherry Pepini had been found. Freshly prepared crispy seasoned chicken that's tossed in a smoky barbecue glaze and topped with a creamy barbecue sauce. Can't picture it? Well, you can try it now at Tim's. Get our new barbecue crispy chicken loaded bowls and wraps for a limited time. Thank you for listening to this episode's ads. By supporting our sponsors, you support Casefile to continue to deliver quality content. By 4.30am on Thanksgiving morning, traffic was already busy on the Interstate 5 highway in Yolo County, a rural area 140 miles south of Reading. As motorists made their way to celebrate the holiday with friends and family, several passers-by noticed something strange on the side of the road.
基思·帕皮尼在黎明前起床开始他的一天。他正在浴室刮胡子时，电话响了。电话那头是负责他妻子案件的侦探之一。他们终于有了消息。雪莉·帕皮尼被找到了。新鲜烹制的脆皮调味鸡肉，裹上烟熏烧烤酱，并淋上奶油烧烤酱。想象不出来吗？好吧，你现在可以在蒂姆（Tim's）尝试一下。在有限的时间内购买我们新的烧烤脆皮鸡肉碗和卷饼。感谢您收听本集的广告。通过支持我们的赞助商，您支持 Casefile 继续提供优质内容。感恩节早晨 4 点 30 分，位于雷丁以南 140 英里的农村地区约洛县（Yolo County）的 5 号州际公路上，交通已经很繁忙。当驾车者前往与亲朋好友庆祝节日时，几位路人注意到路边有些奇怪。

29
00:26:10.000 --> 00:27:13.000
Through the darkness, a panicked looking woman was frantically waving a piece of fabric in the air as though trying to attract attention. Unsure what to make of it, many continued onwards. One woman pulled over a little further down the highway to call 911 while a truck driver pulled over and addressed the woman directly. In a state of distress, she told him her name was Sherry Papini and that she needed an ambulance. She was covered in bruises and said that her vision was blurry. Around her waist was a metal chain. First responders arrived promptly and were shocked by what they saw. The woman who stood before them was a severe contrast to the vibrant smiling face that had been plastered on posters and news bulletins. Sherry Papini was dressed in dirty grey sweatpants, a sweatshirt and socks.
在黑暗中，一名看起来惊慌失措的女子正疯狂地挥舞着一块布，似乎想引起注意。许多人不知道该怎么办，继续前行。一名女子在高速公路前方一点停下车拨打 911，而一名卡车司机停下车直接与该女子交谈。她处于痛苦状态，告诉他她的名字是雪莉·帕皮尼，她需要救护车。她浑身是伤，说她的视力模糊。她的腰间系着一条金属链。急救人员迅速赶到，被他们所看到的景象震惊了。站在他们面前的女子与海报和新闻简报上那个充满活力、面带微笑的脸庞形成了鲜明的对比。雪莉·帕皮尼穿着脏兮兮的灰色运动裤、运动衫和袜子。

30
00:27:13.000 --> 00:28:10.000
Her waist-length blonde hair had been crudely hacked to her shoulders and she looked emaciated. She was disoriented, having no idea where she was or what day it was. There were restraints around her ankles and zip ties around her wrists, one of which was tethered to the chain around her waist. It was only upon being transferred to a nearby hospital that the full extent of Sherry's injuries became clear. Her body was covered in bruises in various states of healing, some yellow and others black and blue. The bridge of her nose was broken and there were rashes and burns all over her arms and legs. Ligature marks were visible on her wrists and ankles. She had lost a little over 10 pounds, a significant amount given she only weighed 105 pounds when she went missing.
她齐腰长的金发被粗暴地剪到了肩膀，看起来骨瘦如柴。她神志不清，不知道自己在哪里，也不知道今天是星期几。她的脚踝上有束缚，手腕上有扎带，其中一个系在腰间的链子上。直到被转移到附近的医院，雪莉受伤的程度才变得清晰起来。她的身体布满了处于不同愈合阶段的淤青，有些是黄色的，有些是青紫色的。她的鼻梁骨折了，手臂和腿上到处都是皮疹和烧伤。手腕和脚踝上有明显的勒痕。她瘦了 10 多磅，考虑到她失踪时只有 105 磅，这是一个相当大的数字。

31
00:28:10.000 --> 00:29:04.000
But the most horrific injury was on her right shoulder. Burnt into her flesh were a series of undistinguishable letters, some scabbed and others already scarred. Sherry had been branded. When Keith Papini arrived at the hospital, it was a teary reunion for the couple. They hugged each other tightly for 20 minutes as Keith was overcome with conflicting emotions. Relief that Sherry had been found alive and revulsion that someone could do something so horrible. Sherry was clearly traumatized and refused to speak to the police. She told Keith that law enforcement had been involved in her abduction and she therefore didn't trust anyone.
但最可怕的伤口是在她的右肩上。烙印在她肉里的是一串无法辨认的字母，有些结了痂，有些已经留下了疤痕。雪莉被烙上了印记。当基思·帕皮尼到达医院时，这对夫妇重逢了，泪流满面。他们紧紧拥抱了 20 分钟，基思被矛盾的情绪所淹没。雪莉活着被找到的宽慰，以及有人能做出如此可怕事情的厌恶。雪莉显然受到了创伤，拒绝与警方交谈。她告诉基思，执法部门参与了她的绑架，因此她不信任任何人。

32
00:29:04.000 --> 00:30:00.000
Instead, investigators gave Keith an audio recorder so that he could ask her questions himself. According to Sherry, she'd been jogging the old Oregon Trail when a dark colored SUV drove by and then backed up again. Two Hispanic women were inside. One of them beckoned her over saying they needed help with something. Sherry approached the vehicle but as she got closer, one of the women held up a small gun. She demanded that Sherry drop her phone and get into the car, reassuring her, we don't want to kill you. Thinking quickly as she removed her headphones, Sherry purposely pulled out several strands of her hair to leave behind as a clue. Sherry got into the vehicle and the women put something over her head.
相反，调查人员给了基思一个录音机，这样他就可以自己问她问题。据雪莉说，她当时正在老俄勒冈小径慢跑，一辆深色的 SUV 开过，然后又倒了回来。车里有两名西班牙裔女性。其中一个向她招手，说她们需要帮忙。雪莉走近车辆，但当她靠近时，其中一名女子举起了一把小枪。她要求雪莉扔掉手机并上车，安慰她说：“我们不想杀你。”雪莉在摘下耳机时灵机一动，故意拔下几缕头发留在身后作为线索。雪莉上了车，女人们用东西蒙住了她的头。

33
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:42.000
One of them struck her with something. Sherry thought it might have been a taser. From there, everything went hazy. She tried to stay awake but kept losing consciousness. The next thing she knew, she woke up in a strange room that had its windows boarded up from the inside. There was nothing in the room except for a bed, a dresser and a closet. All of her clothes were gone and she'd been redressed in a plain t-shirt. Sherry stood on the bed and tried to look out the window only to discover it had also been boarded up from the outside.
其中一个用什么东西打了她。雪莉认为那可能是电击枪。从那以后，一切都变得模糊了。她试图保持清醒，但一直失去知觉。下一件事她知道的是，她在一个奇怪的房间里醒来，窗户从里面被木板封住了。房间里除了床、梳妆台和壁橱外什么都没有。她所有的衣服都不见了，她被换上了一件普通的 T 恤。雪莉站在床上试图向窗外看，却发现窗户也被从外面封住了。

34
00:30:42.000 --> 00:31:43.000
She attempted to dislodge one of the boards but the two women came in and caught her in the act. They yanked her down by her hair and hit her so hard that she saw stars. When Sherry came too, the dresser was gone and the bed was in its place. A chain had been tied around her waist which was bolted to the ceiling and hooked to a metal pole in the closet. Over the coming days, the two women came and went from the room. Sherry was mostly kept locked in the closet. She was given a bucket full of kitty litter to use as a toilet and fed once daily with small portions of bread, gritty rice, porridge and the occasional apple or fad off a piece of meat. Outside her door, a speaker blasted what Sherry described as, quote, that really annoying Mexican music a majority of the time.
她试图撬开其中一块木板，但那两个女人进来抓住了她。她们抓住她的头发把她拽下来，打得她眼冒金星。当雪莉清醒过来时，梳妆台不见了，床取而代之。一条链子系在她的腰上，链子被固定在天花板上，并钩在壁橱里的金属杆上。在接下来的几天里，这两个女人进进出出。雪莉大部分时间都被锁在壁橱里。她得到一桶猫砂作为厕所，每天只吃少量面包、粗米、粥和偶尔的苹果或一块肉。在她的门外，一个扬声器大部分时间都在播放雪莉所描述的“那种非常烦人的墨西哥音乐”。

35
00:31:43.000 --> 00:32:30.000
The two women yelled at her in Spanish which Sherry didn't understand and the older of the two occasionally beat her. Any time Sherry made a sound, she was physically punished. She was sometimes burned with heated up kitchen utensils. When she accidentally made a clanging noise with her chain, one of the women rushed in and cut off her ponytail, threatening, I'm going to send it to your mother. Sherry wasn't particularly close with her mother so this comment led her to believe that her captors didn't know her and had taken her at random. When Sherry questioned why they were doing this, one of them said, We sell you.
这两个女人用雪莉听不懂的西班牙语对她大喊大叫，年纪较大的那个偶尔会殴打她。每当雪莉发出声音，她就会受到身体惩罚。她有时会被加热的厨房用具烫伤。当她不小心用链子发出叮当声时，其中一个女人冲进来剪掉了她的马尾辫，威胁说：“我要把它寄给你妈妈。”雪莉和她母亲的关系并不特别亲密，所以这句话让她认为绑架者不认识她，是随机绑架了她。当雪莉问她们为什么要这样做时，其中一个说：“我们卖了你。”

36
00:32:30.000 --> 00:33:05.000
The other added, your buyer is a cop. The women read Sherry news articles about her disappearance. One of them laughed as she said, No one believes you. Everyone thinks you ran away. Guess what? The buyer is a cop. They're never going to find you. Sherry had no idea what to do. She tried to engage with her captors by offering to cook or clean for them in the hopes they would give her more information.
另一个补充说：“你的买家是警察。”女人们给雪莉读关于她失踪的新闻报道。其中一个笑着说：“没人相信你。每个人都认为你离家出走了。猜猜怎么着？买家是警察。他们永远找不到你。”雪莉不知道该怎么办。她试图通过主动提出为她们做饭或打扫卫生来与绑架者接触，希望她们能给她更多信息。

37
00:33:05.000 --> 00:34:00.000
But the women remained tight-lipped. With Sherry's limited knowledge of Spanish words, she thought she heard mention of traffic, cameras, medicine and a delivery date. Fearful of what that signified, she began making plans to escape. At one point, Sherry's captors forced her into the shower at gunpoint and told her to wash herself. As Sherry lathered herself with coconut-centred body wash, the women became engaged in a conversation and lowered their guns. Recognizing this as an opportunity, Sherry jumped on the younger woman and smashed her head into the toilet. She slipped and cut her foot in the process. The older woman dragged Sherry back to her room by her hair, forcing an unknown substance down her throat.
但女人们守口如瓶。由于雪莉对西班牙语单词的了解有限，她以为听到了关于交通、摄像头、药物和交货日期的提及。担心这意味着什么，她开始计划逃跑。有一次，雪莉的绑架者用枪指着她强迫她洗澡，并告诉她洗干净。当雪莉用椰子味的沐浴露涂抹全身时，女人们开始交谈并放下了枪。意识到这是一个机会，雪莉扑向年轻的那个女人，把她的头撞在马桶上。她在过程中滑倒并割伤了脚。年纪较大的女人抓住雪莉的头发把她拖回房间，强行把一种不明物质灌进她的喉咙。

38
00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:59.000
When Sherry made another attempt to escape, the women tied her to a table and slashed her t-shirt off from behind. Already in agony from her healing breast implants, that's when the women branded her. Sherry's captors told her this is what her buyer wanted. Along with the immense pain, Sherry heard her skin make a sizzling popping sound. Too scared to make a noise, she kept her eyes clenched shut until it was over. While it was unclear what the words said, Sherry believed it said Exodus, which she described as a really confusing Bible passage. To maintain her strength and sanity, Sherry spent some of her spare time doing yoga. She scratched away at the drywall inside the closet in the hopes she might chip a big enough hole to escape.
当雪莉再次尝试逃跑时，女人们把她绑在桌子上，从后面割开了她的 T 恤。由于隆胸手术的伤口还在愈合，她已经痛苦不堪，就在这时，女人们烙印了她。雪莉的绑架者告诉她，这就是她的买家想要的。除了巨大的痛苦，雪莉还听到她的皮肤发出嘶嘶的爆裂声。因为太害怕而不敢出声，她紧闭双眼直到结束。虽然不清楚上面写的是什么字，但雪莉认为写的是“出埃及记”（Exodus），她将其描述为一段非常令人困惑的圣经段落。为了保持体力和理智，雪莉利用空闲时间做瑜伽。她抓挠壁橱里的干墙，希望自己能凿出一个足够大的洞来逃跑。

39
00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:40.000
She thought about her children constantly. Over time, Sherry sensed that the younger of her captors was starting to soften. Sometimes when the older woman beat Sherry, the younger one would drag her off. Then one day, Sherry was sitting on the bed when she heard a gunshot. Terrified, she hid in the closet. It sounded like someone was gathering up keys to leave the house. Then came the blasting mariachi music. Sherry started screaming and yanking on her chains until she eventually fell asleep.
她不断地想念她的孩子们。随着时间的推移，雪莉感觉到年轻的绑架者开始心软了。有时，当年纪较大的女人殴打雪莉时，年轻的那个会把她拉开。有一天，雪莉正坐在床上，听到了一声枪响。她吓坏了，躲进了壁橱。听起来好像有人在收集钥匙准备离开房子。然后是震耳欲聋的墨西哥流浪乐队音乐。雪莉开始尖叫并拉扯她的链子，直到最终睡着了。

40
00:35:40.000 --> 00:36:34.000
When she woke up, the younger of her captors came in and gave her a plate of food. Sherry ate it, but soon started to feel nauseous and dizzy. She could barely stand. The younger captor came back in and hit Sherry in the face. She had laid a fresh sweatsuit out on the bed and insinuated that Sherry get dressed into it. Sherry did so, after which the woman hit her again and placed something over her head so that she couldn't see. Sherry was then let outside and into a vehicle. Sharp restraints were secured around her ankles and wrists, one of which was secured to the vehicle. Sherry didn't know who else was in the car. There were no voices, only the sound of the radio.
当她醒来时，年轻的绑架者进来给了她一盘食物。雪莉吃了，但很快开始感到恶心和头晕。她几乎站不稳。年轻的绑架者回来打了雪莉的脸。她在床上放了一套新的运动服，暗示雪莉换上它。雪莉照做了，之后那个女人又打了她一下，并用东西蒙住了她的头，让她看不见。雪莉随后被带到外面并被塞进一辆车里。尖锐的束缚物被固定在她的脚踝和手腕上，其中一个被固定在车上。雪莉不知道车里还有谁。没有声音，只有收音机的声音。

41
00:36:34.000 --> 00:37:28.000
Sherry tried to keep track of how far they drove by counting the number of songs, but she kept falling asleep. Eventually, the car stopped. The younger captor ordered Sherry to get out. Sherry was terrified. She started crying. The woman cut her restraints, pushed her out the door and drove off. Sherry removed her head covering, realising it was a pillow case. She looked around at her rural surroundings and had no idea where she was. She began to run. Eventually, she came to a building but it was locked, so she started running down the dark highway, waving the pillow case and screaming at the top of her lungs.
雪莉试图通过数歌曲的数量来记录她们开了多远，但她一直睡着。最终，车停了。年轻的绑架者命令雪莉下车。雪莉吓坏了。她开始哭泣。那个女人剪断了她的束缚，把她推下车，然后开车走了。雪莉摘下头罩，意识到那是一个枕套。她环顾四周的农村环境，不知道自己在哪里。她开始奔跑。最终，她来到了一栋建筑前，但门锁着，于是她开始沿着黑暗的高速公路奔跑，挥舞着枕套，声嘶力竭地尖叫。

42
00:37:28.000 --> 00:38:20.000
She screamed so hard that she could taste blood in the back of her throat. Car after car sped past without stopping. Sherry wondered if they could see her restraints and were deterred from stopping because they thought she was an escaped prisoner. She tried to hide them under her clothes until a trucker eventually stopped. Safe in hospital with her husband, Sherry was thoroughly examined. She was adamant that she hadn't endured any form of sexual assault. This was supported by medical exams. Toxicology tests came up clean for narcotics, ruling out the possibility that Sherry had been drugged. Her clothing was sent off for DNA testing.
她尖叫得太用力，以至于能尝到喉咙后部的血腥味。一辆又一辆车飞驰而过，没有停下来。雪莉想知道他们是否看到了她的束缚，并因为认为她是逃犯而不敢停车。她试图把它们藏在衣服下面，直到最终有一辆卡车停了下来。在医院里与丈夫团聚后，雪莉接受了全面检查。她坚称自己没有遭受任何形式的性侵犯。医学检查证实了这一点。毒理学测试显示没有麻醉品，排除了雪莉被下药的可能性。她的衣服被送去进行 DNA 检测。

43
00:38:20.000 --> 00:39:36.000
On Thanksgiving afternoon, members of the Redding community gathered in Sherry's honour as plant, unaware that she'd been found alive. When the good news was revealed a few hours later, Sherry's sister Sheila thanked their supporters, saying, Everyone's tireless efforts have made our family whole again this Thanksgiving. News of Sherry's escape gripped the nation. The public were hungry for details, but the Papini family requested privacy during this time of healing. Over the coming days, investigators gently probed Sherry for any more details she could remember that might help them catch her abductors. While Sherry tried to keep things light-hearted, her trauma was obvious. She hugged her knees to her chest, her eyes mostly cast downward, as she did her best to provide every possible piece of information. The two women had worn masks over the bottom halves of their faces, so Sherry never got a complete look at them, but she remembered other details.
感恩节下午，雷丁社区的成员聚集在一起纪念雪莉，不知道她已经被活着找到了。几个小时后，当好消息传出时，雪莉的妹妹希拉（Sheila）感谢了他们的支持者，她说：“每个人不懈的努力使我们的家庭在这个感恩节再次团聚。”雪莉逃脱的消息震惊了全国。公众渴望了解细节，但帕皮尼一家要求在这一康复期间保持隐私。在接下来的几天里，调查人员温和地询问雪莉是否还能想起任何有助于他们抓住绑架者的细节。虽然雪莉试图让事情变得轻松，但她的创伤显而易见。她双膝抱胸，眼睛大多低垂，尽其所能提供每一条可能的信息。那两个女人在脸的下半部分戴着面具，所以雪莉从未看清她们的全貌，但她记得其他细节。

44
00:39:36.000 --> 00:40:45.000
The older of the pair had a long, straight dark hair that was showing signs of graying. She had dark eyes and thick, bushy eyebrows. She was roughly three inches taller than Sherry, heavyset, and spoke with a raspy voice. Her breath smelled like sweetened coffee. The younger woman had dark curly hair that had been smoothed with product, thin, over-tweased eyebrows, and wore large hoop earrings. She was a bit shorter than Sherry, with a slightly muscular build and hairy arms. Sherry struggled to record details about the clothing either of the women had been wearing, other than the fact they always wore leather gloves. The pair fought often, and Sherry regularly overheard the older woman hit the younger one. As for the location where she was held, Sherry had no idea. She sometimes heard birds outside, but because of the speaker outside her door, she never heard anything else.
年长的那位留着长长的直黑发，已经开始显露灰白。她有着深色的眼睛和浓密粗糙的眉毛。她比雪莉高出大约三英寸，身材魁梧，说话声音沙哑。她的呼吸闻起来有甜味咖啡的味道。年轻的那位留着深色卷发，头发用护发产品梳理得很顺滑，眉毛很细，修剪过度，戴着大圆环耳环。她比雪莉稍矮，体格略显强壮，手臂上有汗毛。雪莉很难记录下这两个女人穿的衣服细节，只记得她们总是戴着皮手套。两人经常吵架，雪莉经常听到年长的女人殴打年轻的那个。至于她被关押的地点，雪莉毫无头绪。她有时能听到外面的鸟叫声，但因为门外有扬声器，她听不到其他任何声音。

45
00:40:45.000 --> 00:41:50.000
It was always cold, possibly raining every night, and she could smell a fireplace. Any time she made a noise, her captors came in and took her blankets away as punishment. The bathroom had a unique layout which Sherry was able to describe in detail, right down to a crack in the shower tile. She never saw the outside of the building. To maintain the integrity of the investigation, police made the strategic decision to withhold details about Sherry's time in captivity, including the branding. But this silence led to speculation from cynics that the whole kidnapping had been a hoax. If the police were so vocal about seeking answers when Sherry went missing, why go quiet when she was returned safely? Was it possible the whole thing had been a publicity stunt by Cameron Gamble, the hostage negotiator after all?
那里总是很冷，可能每天晚上都在下雨，她能闻到壁炉的味道。每当她发出声音，绑架者就会进来拿走她的毯子作为惩罚。浴室的布局很独特，雪莉能详细描述出来，甚至连淋浴瓷砖上的裂缝都记得。她从未见过建筑的外部。为了维护调查的完整性，警方做出战略决定，隐瞒雪莉被囚禁期间的细节，包括烙印。但这种沉默导致愤世嫉俗者猜测整起绑架案是一场骗局。如果警方在雪莉失踪时如此大声疾呼寻求答案，为什么在她安全返回后却保持沉默？难道这一切真的是人质谈判专家卡梅伦·甘布尔策划的宣传噱头吗？

46
00:41:50.000 --> 00:43:00.000
Or perhaps Keith and Sherry had crafted the elaborate plot for financial gain and fame. Investigators had considered this possibility, but unless they had evidence to prove otherwise, they had no reason to treat the abduction as anything other than a legitimate crime. It was a lesson learned the hard way by Vallejo Police, just 180 miles south of Redding. The year before Sherry Papini's abduction, a Vallejo man named Aaron Quinn called police to report a home invasion. He claimed that a gunman had broken into his home and forced him and his girlfriend, Denise Hoskins, to drink tea laced with sleeping pills. They were blindfolded and tied up in the closet, where the gunman played a pre-recorded message. It explained that the couple had been targeted by a criminal group who were going to hold Denise captive, unless Aaron paid an $8,500 ransom within 48 hours. When Aaron woke up hours later, Denise was gone.
或者，也许是基思和雪莉为了经济利益和名声精心策划了这个复杂的阴谋。调查人员考虑过这种可能性，但除非有证据证明事实并非如此，否则他们没有理由将这起绑架案视为合法犯罪以外的事情。这是瓦列霍警方在雷丁以南仅180英里处学到的惨痛教训。在雪莉·帕皮尼被绑架的前一年，一名叫亚伦·奎因的瓦列霍男子报警称家中遭入室抢劫。他声称一名持枪歹徒闯入家中，强迫他和女友丹妮丝·霍斯金斯喝下掺有安眠药的茶。他们被蒙住双眼并绑在壁橱里，歹徒播放了一段预先录制的信息。信息解释说，这对夫妇被一个犯罪团伙盯上，如果亚伦不在48小时内支付8500美元赎金，他们就会扣押丹妮丝。当亚伦几小时后醒来时，丹妮丝已经不见了。

47
00:43:00.000 --> 00:44:11.000
He reported the incident to police, but the story was so outlandish that they thought he was making it up. When Denise resurfaced two days later claiming to have been held captive and raped, both law enforcement and the media palmed it off as a wild hoax. Three months later, police were investigating an unrelated home invasion when they uncovered evidence linking the perpetrator to Denise Hoskins and Aaron Quinn. It turned out the couple had been telling the truth. The perpetrator, a disbarred attorney named Matthew Muller, was tried and sentenced to 31 years in prison. Vallejo police were forced to publicly apologize to Denise and Aaron, who were awarded a $2.5 million compensation payout. Investigators in the Sherry Papini case were determined not to make a similar mistake. Keith Papini released an exclusive statement to national news program Good Morning America to address the rumors surrounding his wife's case head-on.
他向警方报告了这起事件，但故事太离奇，警方认为他在编造。当丹妮丝两天后重新出现，声称自己被囚禁并遭到强奸时，执法部门和媒体都将其视为一场荒唐的骗局。三个月后，警方在调查一起无关的入室抢劫案时，发现了将肇事者与丹妮丝·霍斯金斯和亚伦·奎因联系起来的证据。事实证明，这对夫妇说的是真话。肇事者是一名被吊销执照的律师，名叫马修·穆勒，他被审判并判处31年监禁。瓦列霍警方被迫公开向丹妮丝和亚伦道歉，并向他们支付了250万美元的赔偿金。雪莉·帕皮尼案的调查人员决心不再犯同样的错误。基思·帕皮尼向全国新闻节目《早安美国》发表了一份独家声明，正面回应了围绕他妻子案件的传言。

48
00:44:11.000 --> 00:45:16.000
He acknowledged the quote, double-edged sword that is social media. While modern technology had allowed news of Sherry's disappearance to spread quickly, those same people who helped spread the word now expected answers instantly and became angry when they didn't get the gory details. Keith said, Those people should be ashamed of their malicious subhuman behavior. We are not going to allow those people to take away our spirit, love or rejoice in our girl found alive and home where she belongs. I do not see a purpose in addressing each preposterous lie. Instead, may I give you a glimpse of the mixture of horror and elation that was my experience of reuniting with the love of my life and mother of our children. Keith went on to provide a harrowing account of Sherry's ordeal, complete with the details of her injuries, including the branding.
他承认了社交媒体这把“双刃剑”。虽然现代科技让雪莉失踪的消息迅速传播，但那些曾经帮助传播消息的人现在却期望立即得到答案，并在得不到血腥细节时感到愤怒。基思说：“那些人应该为他们这种恶毒的非人行为感到羞耻。我们不会允许这些人夺走我们的精神、爱，也不会允许他们对我们的女孩活着回来并回到她所属的家中感到幸灾乐祸。我不认为回应每一个荒谬的谎言有什么意义。相反，让我带你们一窥我与我一生的挚爱、我们孩子的母亲重逢时那种恐惧与狂喜交织的经历。”基思随后讲述了雪莉遭受的痛苦折磨，包括她受伤的细节，以及烙印的情况。

49
00:45:16.000 --> 00:46:21.000
He remarked, Nothing could have prepared me for what I was about to see upon my arrival at the hospital, nor the details of the true hell I was about to hear. Acknowledging the tireless support of law enforcement and the public, Keith said, Thank you to the many incredible humans that have never known Sherry that facilitated in sharing our heartbreak across the globe. Sherry has always captured my heart, and it is no surprise that she has captured hearts not only through the country, but throughout the world. The following day, police held a press conference to acknowledge Sherry Papini's courage. They released brief details about her two captors and appealed for anyone with information to come forward. The fact that Sherry had overheard the perpetrators talking about a buyer and getting paid gave weight to the human trafficking theory.
他感叹道：“当我到达医院时，没有什么能让我为即将看到的一切做好准备，也没有什么能让我为即将听到的真实地狱般的细节做好准备。”在感谢执法部门和公众的不懈支持时，基思说：“感谢许多从未认识雪莉却帮助我们在全球范围内分享我们心碎经历的不可思议的人们。雪莉一直占据着我的心，她不仅俘获了全国人民的心，也俘获了全世界人民的心，这并不令人惊讶。”第二天，警方举行新闻发布会，表彰雪莉·帕皮尼的勇气。他们发布了关于两名绑架者的简要细节，并呼吁任何有信息的人挺身而出。雪莉无意中听到绑架者谈论买家和获得报酬的事实，为人口贩卖理论增加了分量。

50
00:46:21.000 --> 00:47:15.000
Maybe the women had kidnapped Sherry at random, thinking she was much younger. When they realized she was a 34-year-old mother, they didn't know how to proceed, hence why they held her captive for so long and were constantly bickering. But if this was the case, it would be highly unusual. In the United States, white women are rarely abducted for sex trafficking. Victims usually know their exploiters, who are often tricked into willingly going with them after being promised a better life. Perpetrators involved are typically professionals. It would be highly unusual for someone involved in trafficking to let a victim go, as it risked exposing the entire ring. The fact that Sherry was branded also raised questions.
也许这两个女人是随机绑架了雪莉，以为她年轻得多。当她们意识到她是一位34岁的母亲时，她们不知道该如何处理，这就是为什么她们把她关押了这么久，而且一直在争吵。但如果真是这样，那将是非常罕见的。在美国，白人女性很少因性贩卖而被绑架。受害者通常认识剥削者，他们往往在被承诺更好的生活后被诱骗自愿跟随。涉及的肇事者通常是专业人士。对于参与贩卖的人来说，释放受害者是非常罕见的，因为这冒着暴露整个团伙的风险。雪莉被烙印的事实也引发了疑问。

51
00:47:15.000 --> 00:48:25.000
Some believed this type of torture was typical for traffickers who wanted to maintain control over their victim, while others questioned why a sex trafficker would want to taint their own product. Based on the description that Sherry had provided of her time in captivity, investigators began working on the theory that she had been held somewhere in the mountains. They obtained cell phone data from the area where Sherry was abducted and the area where she was found, on the lookout for any numbers that pinged off phone towers at both locations. As reported by the Sacramento Bee, six numbers came up. Among them was a 21-year-old woman. Police visited her home, discovering that she had dark hair like Sherry's young captor, but she wasn't Latina and had an alibi for the abduction period. Tip-offs continued to come in from the public. One woman reported having seen a pair of Latina women who matched the suspect descriptions in a Walmart store.
有些人认为这种酷刑是那些想要维持对受害者控制的贩卖者的典型做法，而另一些人则质疑为什么性贩卖者会想要玷污自己的“产品”。根据雪莉提供的关于她被囚禁期间的描述，调查人员开始推测她被关在山里的某个地方。他们获取了雪莉被绑架区域和她被发现区域的手机数据，寻找在两个地点都连接过手机信号塔的任何号码。据《萨克拉门托蜜蜂报》报道，出现了六个号码。其中一个是21岁的女性。警方走访了她的家，发现她有着像雪莉年轻绑架者那样的深色头发，但她不是拉丁裔，并且有绑架期间的不在场证明。公众提供的线索不断涌入。一名女子报告说在沃尔玛超市看到了一对符合嫌疑人描述的拉丁裔女性。

52
